# env for deploy/compose/docker-compose.full.yaml — the full, nothing-in-memory, Temporal-backed stack.
#   cp deploy/compose/.env.full.example deploy/compose/.env
#   docker compose -f deploy/compose/docker-compose.full.yaml --env-file deploy/compose/.env up -d --build
#
# Required before first `up`: POSTGRES_PASSWORD, MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD, EVERDICT_SECRETS_KEY, EVERDICT_INTERNAL_TOKEN.
# (Or skip hand-editing entirely: `bash deploy/compose/full.sh` creates this file and generates every required secret.)
# For a working chat/teammates, also set a model for the agent (AGENT_MODEL or AGENT_LLM_*) — see that section below.

# ── Image tags (GHCR api/web/agent). Ignored under `up --build` (builds from source). ──
# Each service is released on its OWN tag (`api-v1.2.0` → everdict-api:1.2.0), so each one pins separately.
# EVERDICT_VERSION is the fallback every unset service falls back to — leave the per-service lines empty to run
# the whole stack at one version, or fill one in to move a single service without touching the rest.
EVERDICT_VERSION=latest
EVERDICT_API_VERSION=
EVERDICT_WEB_VERSION=
EVERDICT_AGENT_VERSION=

# ── Ports (host side) ──────────────────────────────────────────
WEB_PORT=3001
API_PORT=8787
AGENT_PORT=8790
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
TEMPORAL_PORT=7233
TEMPORAL_UI_PORT=8233
KEYCLOAK_PORT=8080

# ── Postgres (shared by the control plane AND Temporal) — password REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_USER=everdict
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-postgres
POSTGRES_DB=everdict

# ── Temporal image tags — pin these; verify the tags exist for your platform before first run ──────────────────
# auto-setup follows Temporal server releases (e.g. 1.26.2 / 1.27.2). ui follows its own line (e.g. 2.34.0).
TEMPORAL_VERSION=1.27.2
TEMPORAL_UI_VERSION=2.34.0

# ── MinIO object storage — the WORKSPACE FILESYSTEM + artifact offload — password REQUIRED ─────────────────────
# The filesystem is bucket-per-tenant (`everdict-fs-<tenant>-<hash8>`, created lazily; skill/knowledge bodies +
# agent task outputs + the web /files tree live there). Run media offloads to EVERDICT_S3_BUCKET (presigned URLs).
MINIO_ROOT_USER=everdict
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me-minio
# Host ports: S3 API / web console (inspect a tenant's bucket from the console).
MINIO_PORT=9100
MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=9101
# Image tag pin (minio/minio release).
MINIO_VERSION=RELEASE.2024-12-18T13-15-44Z
# Artifact bucket (single, run media) + the per-tenant filesystem bucket-name prefix.
EVERDICT_S3_BUCKET=everdict-artifacts
EVERDICT_S3_FS_BUCKET_PREFIX=everdict-fs
# Presigned ARTIFACT links (run screenshots/DOM) are minted against the in-network endpoint (http://minio:9000),
# which an off-host browser cannot resolve. Set a browser-reachable base (like API_PUBLIC_URL, e.g.
# http://<host-ip>:9100) and the links are SIGNED for it — SigV4 covers the host, so this cannot be patched onto
# the URL afterwards (that answers 403 SignatureDoesNotMatch). The workspace filesystem and the scorecard analysis
# download are served through the api — they need no public MinIO.
MINIO_PUBLIC_URL=

# ── Managed image store (optional — bring it up with `--profile images`) ───────────
# everdict's OWN registry for environment images: the workspace gets a namespace the moment it exists, and the
# control plane mints the pull/push grants (no BYO registry, no credentials to register). Unset ENDPOINT = the
# deployment is BYO-only and /v2/token 404s. Design: docs/architecture/managed-image-store.md
# ⚠️ Both of these must be reachable from EVERY machine that pulls — a self-hosted runner on someone's laptop
# included. localhost is correct for a single-host stack and wrong the moment a second machine is involved.
# ENDPOINT is what image REFS carry (<endpoint>/<workspace-namespace>/<name>); REALM is what the registry hands
# the docker client as the place to exchange its grant.
IMAGE_STORE_ENDPOINT=
IMAGE_STORE_REALM=
IMAGE_STORE_PORT=5001
IMAGE_STORE_S3_BUCKET=everdict-images
# Grant lifetime (seconds, default 3600). A dispatched job's pull credentials are minted BEFORE it is queued, so
# this must cover queue wait + pull — not just the token exchange. Lower it to tighten how fast revoked reach
# stops working; a job queued past it fails at pull with the registry's own error (visible, not silent).
IMAGE_STORE_GRANT_TTL_SECONDS=3600
# `full.sh --profile images` generates deploy/compose/certs/image-token.{key,crt} (gitignored) and never rotates
# them: a new key invalidates every grant already in flight.

# ── Control-plane API — REQUIRED secrets ───────────────────────
# Secret at-rest encryption KEK (base64, 32 bytes):  openssl rand -base64 32
EVERDICT_SECRETS_KEY=
# Guard token for /internal/** (Temporal worker→API bridge + tenant-key minting):  openssl rand -hex 32
EVERDICT_INTERNAL_TOKEN=

# Idle timeout (ms) before a parked self-hosted job with no lease/heartbeat is rejected as no_runner. Default 5 min.
EVERDICT_SELF_HOSTED_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_MS=300000

# ── Trace ledger (the OWNED trajectory store) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everdict keeps its own copy of every trace it stands on — eval runs, AGENT conversation turns (a transcript is a
# trace), OTLP-door arrivals (POST /v1/traces), and materialized pull-imports. Browse it in Settings › Traces.
# Empty EVERDICT_CLICKHOUSE_URL = rung 1: the ledger lives in Postgres (DATABASE_URL) — the default, and enough
# for eval-scale. For ops-scale volume, bring up the bundled engine and point the api at it:
#   EVERDICT_CLICKHOUSE_URL=http://clickhouse:8123
#   docker compose -f deploy/compose/docker-compose.full.yaml --env-file deploy/compose/.env --profile clickhouse up -d
# ONLY this store moves; every other store stays on Postgres. The table is created at boot (no migration step).
# ⚠️ Switching engines does NOT copy what is already sealed — old trajectories stay in Postgres and disappear from
#    the ledger until you switch back. Switch on an empty ledger, or accept the gap knowingly.
# ⚠️ The URL and the profile travel TOGETHER. A URL set without `--profile clickhouse` means the api boots against
#    an engine that is not running, fails applying its DDL, and restarts forever. Clear the URL to go back to rung 1.
EVERDICT_CLICKHOUSE_URL=
# ClickHouse database name (empty = the server default).
EVERDICT_CLICKHOUSE_DATABASE=
# OTLP-door admission: events accepted per workspace per rolling hour (empty = unlimited). Past the bound the door
# answers 429 and lands trace.ingestion_throttled on the event log — never a silent drop. A workspace can set a
# LOWER limit for itself in Settings; it can never exceed this operator default.
EVERDICT_INGEST_MAX_EVENTS_PER_HOUR=
# Ledger retention in days (empty = keep forever). A daily sweep deletes trajectories sealed before the cutoff and
# logs how many went. Scores/verdicts are separate records and are NOT deleted with the evidence.
EVERDICT_TRAJECTORY_RETENTION_DAYS=

# ── Conversational agent (the assistant behind the web chat + proactive teammates) ─────────────────────────────
# The agent MUST have a model to answer. Set EXACTLY ONE of the two options below; with neither, the agent
# container fails fast on boot (web/api still come up — only the chat is down).
#
# Option A (preferred) — a registered workspace model id. Register the model in the app (Settings › Models) with its
#   provider API key as a workspace secret; the agent resolves it per request against Postgres + EVERDICT_SECRETS_KEY.
AGENT_MODEL=
# Option B — a raw OpenAI-compatible endpoint (LiteLLM / vLLM). For a proxy on the Docker HOST use host.docker.internal.
AGENT_LLM_BASE_URL=
AGENT_LLM_API_KEY=
AGENT_LLM_MODEL=
#
# Proactive teammates (S4): the api pushes run/scorecard completions to the agent so watching teammates wake. This
# token guards that path and MUST match on both services (it is injected into api AND agent). Empty → disabled
# (chat still works; only unsolicited teammate wake-ups are off).  openssl rand -hex 32
AGENT_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
#
# Optional — let the agent DRIVE eval (run/retry scorecards, register/pin harnesses, …). Every call is still
# HITL/plan/rule-gated and RBAC-bounded. Empty/false → read-only + integration surface only.
AGENT_ALLOW_EVAL_DRIVE=
# Optional — built-in web_search (Tavily) for every workspace's agent out of the box (else a workspace supplies its own).
AGENT_WEBSEARCH_API_KEY=
# Optional — model tiering (registered model ids like AGENT_MODEL): cheaper models for compaction / transient-failure
# fallback / spawned sub-agents. Empty → all reuse AGENT_MODEL.
AGENT_SMALL_MODEL=
AGENT_FALLBACK_MODEL=
AGENT_SUBAGENT_MODEL=
# Optional — extended-thinking budget (tokens; >1024), per-tool deadline (ms), agentic-loop turn cap. Empty → engine defaults.
AGENT_THINKING_BUDGET=
AGENT_TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS=
AGENT_MAX_TURNS=

# ── Externally reachable URLs ──────────────────────────────────
# The API base reachable from OUTSIDE the compose network — used for: the front-door callback rendezvous target,
# GitHub App install callback, Mattermost inbound, and live-trace deep-links. On a real host use its LAN IP/DNS,
# NOT localhost (a self-hosted runner on another machine must reach it). Leave empty to fall back to http://api:8787
# (only works for in-network topology backends; off-host self-hosted runners then can't post callbacks).
API_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8787
# The web base the browser is sent back to (Auth.js AUTH_URL) AND the base every link the product hands out is built
# from — invite links, Mattermost/GitHub notifications, and the links the conversational agent gives members. Set it to
# the URL MEMBERS actually browse (the host's LAN IP/DNS); localhost is right only when the browser is on this host.
WEB_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001
# The control plane's WebSocket base as the BROWSER dials it (live browser session, run screen, run terminal).
# Empty is right for the ordinary single-host deploy: the web rebases the internal `api:8787` host onto the host
# the browser asked for. Set it only when the control plane is published somewhere else — behind a reverse proxy
# or on another host — e.g. wss://everdict.example.com/api.
CONTROL_PLANE_WS_URL=

# ── Optional: limits / managed backend / local claude-code run auth ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-tenant concurrent-run ceiling (empty = unlimited).
EVERDICT_TENANT_RUNS=
# Agent image for managed (nomad/k8s) backends — not needed for local/self-hosted execution.
EVERDICT_AGENT_IMAGE=
# Only if the local backend runs the claude-code harness in-process (can be replaced by workspace secrets).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Optional: interactive browser sessions (browser login profiles) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off by default. Set 1 to enable the interactive login browser + profile capture (Settings › Browser profiles).
EVERDICT_BROWSER_SESSIONS=
# Provisioner. RECOMMENDED for this containerized stack: `remote` — the api LEASES a whole browser from the
# `browser` sidecar pool over the compose network. No Docker socket, no host Chrome. Start the sidecar with the
# `browser` compose profile:  docker compose -f docker-compose.full.yaml --profile browser up -d
# (`docker` instead launches a container per session — needs the socket mount on the api AND a host-run control
#  plane; leave empty to fall back to the dev host-Chrome provisioner.)
EVERDICT_BROWSER_PROVISIONER=remote
# remote pool: comma-separated CDP bases of the browser sidecars (reachable from the api by service name). Add
# more sidecars (browser2, browser3, …) and list them here to raise concurrency — one browser is leased per session.
EVERDICT_BROWSER_CDP_POOL=http://browser:9222
# Browser image override (air-gapped/mirror deployments; digest-pinned) — empty = the pinned default image. Applies
# to both the `browser` sidecar (remote) and the launched container (docker).
EVERDICT_BROWSER_IMAGE=
# `docker` provisioner only: the network the launched browser container joins (must be one the api is on).
EVERDICT_BROWSER_DOCKER_NETWORK=
# Live-session caps, 429 beyond (empty = unlimited). For `remote`, keep the fleet cap <= the number of sidecars.
EVERDICT_BROWSER_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_TENANT=
EVERDICT_BROWSER_MAX_SESSIONS=

# ── Optional: workspace GitHub App (github.com) ────────────────
# Create at https://github.com/settings/apps. Setup URL = ${API_PUBLIC_URL}/workspace/github-app/callback.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=   # PEM; base64(PEM) recommended for single-line env-file safety
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=

# ── Optional: workspace GitHub App (GitHub Enterprise) ─────────
# ONE App on the single enterprise host for the whole deployment, handled identically to github.com
# (install-only — workspaces just click install + pick repos). All four required to enable.
GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_HOST=   # e.g. https://ghe.example.com
GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_APP_ID=
GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_APP_SLUG=
GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=   # PEM; base64(PEM) recommended for single-line env-file safety

# ── Optional: workspace Mattermost notifications ───────────────
# Operator-configured server URL; workspaces register only a bot token + channel in Settings › Integrations.
MATTERMOST_HOST=   # e.g. https://mattermost.example.com

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AUTH (multi-tenant SSO) — leave this whole block empty for single tenant=default (no login).
# To enable: fill the values below AND start with `--profile auth`, e.g.
#   docker compose -f deploy/compose/docker-compose.full.yaml --profile auth up -d --build
#
# ⚠️ Keycloak issuer must resolve to the SAME URL from the browser AND from the api/web containers.
#    `localhost` does NOT satisfy this (inside a container localhost = the container itself). Set PUBLIC_HOST to a
#    real host/IP reachable from both (e.g. your machine's LAN IP, or a hostname you add to /etc/hosts), and update
#    deploy/keycloak/realm-everdict.json redirectUris/webOrigins to that origin (currently http://localhost:3001).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PUBLIC_HOST=192.168.1.50
# EVERDICT_REQUIRE_AUTH=1
# KEYCLOAK_ADMIN=admin
# KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin
# API side (JWT verification):
# KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=http://192.168.1.50:8080/realms/everdict
# OIDC_AUDIENCE=
# WORKSPACE_CLAIM=workspace
# Web side (Auth.js token courier) — client id/secret come from realm-everdict.json:
# AUTH_SECRET=            # openssl rand -base64 32
# KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=everdict-web
# KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=everdict-web-secret

# ── Optional web extras ────────────────────────────────────────
# Temporal UI deep link — unset defaults to http://localhost:${TEMPORAL_UI_PORT}; the web rebases a loopback
# host onto the browser's request host, so the default works for remote users. Set only to pin a vanity/proxied URL.
# TEMPORAL_UI_URL=http://localhost:8233
# DESKTOP_DOWNLOAD_URL=https://github.com/everdict/everdict/releases/latest
